WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.013
Each year, five million Americans

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:03.642
get their wisdom teeth removed,

00:00:03.642 --> 00:00:04.667
which costs about

00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:08.072
three billion dollars
in total medical costs.

00:00:08.072 --> 00:00:10.547
But for many, it's worth it,

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.739
since leaving them in can
cause serious problems

00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:17.597
like gum infection, tooth
decay, and even tumors.

00:00:17.626 --> 00:00:18.459
But wisdom teeth

00:00:18.459 --> 00:00:21.117
weren't always the unwelcome
threat we see today.

00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:26.957
Wisdom teeth have been around
for millennia.

00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:27.885
Our ancient ancestors

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:30.907
used them the same way we
use our other eight molars:

00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:32.324
to grind up food,

00:00:32.335 --> 00:00:35.445
which was especially handy
before the advent of cooking

00:00:35.445 --> 00:00:37.302
around seven thousand years ago,

00:00:37.302 --> 00:00:39.459
back when our diet consisted of raw meat

00:00:39.459 --> 00:00:43.292
and plants that were fibrous
and tough to chew.

00:00:43.851 --> 00:00:47.189
But once we got our hands
on softer cooked foods,

00:00:47.189 --> 00:00:50.038
our powerful jaws no longer
needed to work as hard

00:00:50.038 --> 00:00:52.457
and shrank as a result.

00:00:52.457 --> 00:00:53.867
But here's the problem:

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:56.697
The genes that determine
the size of our jaws

00:00:56.697 --> 00:00:59.193
are completely separate from
the genes that determine

00:00:59.193 --> 00:01:01.220
how many teeth we grow.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.419
So as our jaws shrank,

00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:05.586
we still kept all 32 teeth.

00:01:05.586 --> 00:01:06.818
And it eventually got to the point

00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:10.823
where there wasn't enough
space to fit all of the teeth.

00:01:10.823 --> 00:01:14.585
But why did wisdom teeth
specifically get the boot?

00:01:14.585 --> 00:01:18.501
Well, they're the last
to show up to the party.

00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:22.618
Wisdom teeth don't usually
grow in until you're between

00:01:22.618 --> 00:01:25.373
16 and 18 years old.

00:01:25.373 --> 00:01:28.230
And by that time, chances
are your other 28 teeth

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:33.054
have taken up all the
available space in your mouth.

00:01:33.054 --> 00:01:33.887
In that case,

00:01:33.887 --> 00:01:35.881
instead of growing in like a normal tooth

00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:39.646
wisdom teeth get trapped
or impacted in your jaw,

00:01:39.646 --> 00:01:42.345
which often makes them
grow in at odd angles

00:01:42.345 --> 00:01:44.603
and press against your back molars

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.186
causing pain and swelling.

00:01:47.186 --> 00:01:50.212
It also forms a narrow
crevice between the teeth

00:01:50.212 --> 00:01:52.795
creating the perfect food trap.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.831
This makes the tooth difficult to clean

00:01:55.831 --> 00:01:58.164
which attracts more bacteria

00:01:58.186 --> 00:02:00.727
and can cause infection and tooth decay,

00:02:00.727 --> 00:02:04.608
eventually leading to gum
disease if left untreated.

00:02:04.608 --> 00:02:06.213
But it gets worse.

00:02:06.221 --> 00:02:09.502
Tooth decay can eventually
destroy your wisdom tooth.

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:11.289
So, to save you and your teeth

00:02:11.289 --> 00:02:12.872
from such a horrible fate,

00:02:12.872 --> 00:02:15.214
dentists will often remove wisdom teeth

00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:17.380
before they go rogue.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.587
Seems reasonable, right?

00:02:19.603 --> 00:02:21.920
Well, it's actually a controversial topic

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.621
among some in the dental community.

00:02:24.621 --> 00:02:25.920
The worry is that we're removing

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.061
our wisdom teeth too frequently,

00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:30.143
often when it's unnecessary

00:02:30.143 --> 00:02:32.106
and the teeth pose no threat,

00:02:32.106 --> 00:02:33.751
like if your mouth is big enough

00:02:33.751 --> 00:02:36.096
or you're one of the 38 percent of people

00:02:36.096 --> 00:02:39.363
who don't develop all four wisdom teeth.

00:02:39.405 --> 00:02:41.597
In that case,
risks from surgery

00:02:41.605 --> 00:02:43.920
like infection and nerve damage

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:46.980
pose more danger
than the teeth themselves.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.730
But the fact remains.

00:02:48.759 --> 00:02:50.886
When wisdom teeth do
become a problem,

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:54.320
you'll curse the day we invented cooking.

